# Pinned versions of the embedded tailnet spikes (ADR 0040, plan s8 unit T0). Spike only.
#
# The desktop spike (plan s4 unit T0, ADR 0037 D9) uses the same pins, so both platforms build
# one libtailscale. Change them together, and only after a check of Tailscale's security
# bulletins (https://tailscale.com/security-bulletins).
#
# - GO_TOOLCHAIN: the go command runs exactly this toolchain (GOTOOLCHAIN). An older go on PATH
#   downloads it and checks it against sum.golang.org. libtailscale at the commit below needs
#   go 1.27.1 or later (its go.mod); 1.27.3 is the newest patch release on 2026-11-03.
# - LIBTAILSCALE_COMMIT: github.com/tailscale/libtailscale, "mark handed-out fds close-on-exec"
#   (2026-10-30). It contains the fix for TS-2026-012 (the SCM_RIGHTS record framing of
#   258321b9).
# - TAILSCALE_MODULE_VERSION: the tailscale.com version in that commit's go.mod and go.sum. The
#   build fails when the checkout names another version. v1.104.5 is the newest patch release;
#   the bulletins after v1.104.1 (TS-2026-016, TS-2026-017) are about Serve, which the spike
#   does not use. T1 decides on a bump with its own go.sum.
# - GO_LICENSES_MODULE: the go-licenses report of plan T0 (a second opinion; the build's own
#   check is scripts/licenses.py).
GO_TOOLCHAIN=go1.27.3
LIBTAILSCALE_REPO=https://github.com/tailscale/libtailscale.git
LIBTAILSCALE_COMMIT=ac7ed43af14e19e1c1810ee9f8319872c6beb412
TAILSCALE_MODULE_VERSION=v1.104.1
GO_LICENSES_MODULE=github.com/google/go-licenses/v2@v2.0.1
IOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET=26.0
